  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "A two-hour delay means school, work, or transport services start 120 minutes later than their regularly scheduled time. Bus pickups, classes, and morning programs typically operate exactly two hours later than normal, while afternoon sessions often continue on their regular schedule. Key Aspects of a 2-Hour Delay: School Start Times: If school usually starts at 8:00 a.m., it will start at 10:00 a.m.. Bus Pickups: Morning bus pickups are delayed by two hours (e.g., 7:10 a.m. becomes 9:10 a.m.). Programs/Childcare: Morning preschool or half-day programs are often canceled, while full-day programs and afternoon sessions may still run. Attendance: Breakfast is usually still served, and lunch is typically provided at the regular time. Procedures: Parents and staff should check local school district websites, social media, or school hotlines for official, up-to-date notifications. Be sure to monitor local alerts, as a 2-hour delay can sometimes be updated to a full school closure if conditions do not improve.",
